WEBVTT

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:17.950
All set.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:19.950
Sis!

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.740
If you don't get up, you'll be late!

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.210
What the...

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.210
After you got home drunk, 
you drank some more?

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:32.340
Man, you're so hopeless...

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.050
<b>organizational backing</b>

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.010
I made you French toast, okay?

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.060
Thanks, Hinata...

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.620
I'm gonna get going.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.270
Take care.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.820
Oh, today is recycling day.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.400
Take out the cans and bottles, okay?

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:48.900
Don't forget!

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:53.030
So sleepy.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.660
<i>In response to an increase in heinous crimes,</i>

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:07.170
<i>a new movement is picking up steam in police 
and security forces around the world.</i>

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.170
<i>This is the story of the services 
performed by ACTIVE in Japan.</i>

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.580
<b>File 2: Academy Destruction</b>

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.500
<i>Morning!</i>

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.570
<i>Welcome to Liko's TV program guide!</i>

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:36.320
<i>Do you want the usual?</i>

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.610
<i>Okay, </i>Morning Electro-Circus<i> it is!</i>

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:43.140
Hinata went and installed some weird app again.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:50.600
<b>Police Department 
Big Showdown on Expressway 

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:47.510
<i>So, their flamboyant arrest act 
destroyed the expressway,</i>

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.600
<i>resulting in partial blockage of Yamate Avenue.</i>

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:56.110
<i>Let's hear what Manabe Youichi-san, a former 
defense official and police expert, has to say.</i>

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:00.860
<i>Manabe-san, Unit 8, Japan's ACTIVE, 
has overstepped its bound yet again.</i>

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:07.120
<b>Police Department 
Big Showdown on Expressway</b>

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.940
<i>Well, there are many factors to consider.</i>

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.700
<i>Given that the criminals 
were armed to the teeth,</i>

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.080
<i>you're forced to respond 
in kind, to a certain point.</i>

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.130
<i>So you're saying excessive force is necessary.</i>

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.960
<i>That's not quite what I said.</i>

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:18.550
<b>Police Department 
Big Showdown on Expressway</b>

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.630
<i>What about you, Ishiguro-san?</i>

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.080
<i>It's way over the top. What a bunch of clowns.</i>

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:23.010
<i>How much of our tax money 
are they going to waste?</i>

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.600
<i>We requested an interview with the police,</i>

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.660
<i>but they only gave us their usual line.</i>

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:32.900
<i>"Our understanding is that Unit 8 has upheld the 
law with their actions, which were blameless."</i>

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.610
<i>"We will refrain from publicly commenting 
on specifics, due to national security."</i>

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.610
They call us at the first sign of trouble, 
but they're still territorial, huh?

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.700
<b>Distance to Destination: 2.5km</b>

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.540
Good morning.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:03.050
Well, if no one's here, 
it's easier to snoop around.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:09.680
Red alert! We have an emergency sortie request 
from Okinawa's Naha Police Department.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.630
Please equip Willwear.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:12.510
Roger.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.480
Wait, why is it Kyoukai-san?

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:21.930
Please hurry!

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:23.200
I know.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.820
Your Willwear is ready.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.580
Brief me on the case while I change.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.430
Huh?

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:30.930
Oh, uh, right...

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:34.000
The famous aquarium was attacked.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.160
Churaumi?

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.860
That isn't Naha's jurisdiction. It's Ishikawa's.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.520
Huh?

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.090
Uh, the attackers fled to Naha Airport by sea...

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.610
The emergency sortie request is a lie, isn't it?

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:50.250
Oops, you got me.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.220
Why are you barging in here?!

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.350
Oh, don't worry.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.770
I don't get turned on by that kind of "inner" suit.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.270
That's not the issue here!

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:02.890
I thought we should customize 
your new Wear, that's all.

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:04.530
Thanks, but no thanks!

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:05.990
Oh, but...

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.900
Even without your unwanted help,

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.200
I've already memorized the manual!

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.540
But your Wear is from the Wakaba Group—

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.310
I don't need you to explain it to me!

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:15.540
Hey!

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.290
Let me at least do the Wear's data graph—

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.730
I understand why you need the data,

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:25.170
given that you're from the Willwear association.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:29.640
But if you're looking to customize mine, 
please take care of the battery first.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.350
I don't want to go through what Sena-san did!

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:40.040
I guess trying to force customization 
was the wrong move...

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:54.250
Those with means grow ever richer,

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.710
while those without grow ever poorer.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:05:59.660
Ask,

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:01.840
and it will be given to you.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.340
<b><i>Kouki Education Academy</i></b>

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.810
Good morning, president!

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:10.250
Oh, good morning, Yamabuki-kun.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:13.140
I e-mailed you the council meeting agenda.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.430
Please review it.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:15.720
All right.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.810
You work fast, Yamabuki-kun.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:20.330
Thank you!

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.950
<b>Safety First</b>

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.220
Kouki Education Academy, in Shinagawa...

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.670
Why is no one here?

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:50.370
It's already nine o'clock!

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:52.570
Isn't anyone on call? 
What's up with this unit?!

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:55.680
<b>Report Form</b>

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:55.680
I'll report this lack of discipline to HQ!

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:57.760
Morning!

00:06:57.760 --> 00:06:59.020
Good morning.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:01.210
You're here early, Asami-chan.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:03.040
Relatively speaking, I suppose I am.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.110
Here we go!

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.110
<b>Towing</b>

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.790
Um, what's that?

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:18.430
It's a super rare LED bus sign that says "Towing."

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:23.080
Liko-chan told me there was a sighting this 
morning, so I just had to rush over!

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.900
Good job, Liko-chan.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.840
That's the reason you're late?

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:31.110
I got permission from the section chief.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:34.020
He said everyone except you would be late.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.280
He, himself, will get in after noon.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:38.350
Even the boss?!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.390
<b>Saitama Prefecture Oomiya Police Station</b>

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:40.390
I'm so sorry.

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:46.020
We did request backup, so I don't want 
to make an issue of it, but...

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:46.570
Go ahead.

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:50.820
Will it always be on us to
write the letter of apology?

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.800
I apologize.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:57.830
Regulations stipulate that we always 
operate by official request, so...

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:01.150
We have a bunch of quicksand refugees 
from Tokyo, you know.

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.660
We're in a crunch here.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:04.920
I am well aware of that.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.410
I believe we've previously made a point

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:10.300
of requesting speedier arrests.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:13.290
I apologize. The perpetrators' Willwear units

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:16.660
were modified beyond what could be foreseen.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.110
I'm not asking for excuses.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.080
I am truly, truly sorry...

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.850
I chose you because

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.900
you remain calm and collected.

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:29.840
You don't rashly pursue justice.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:33.610
You apprehend criminals within the 
bounds prescribed by the law.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:36.670
That's how I'd assessed you, at least.

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:40.870
I understand there can be many 
unforeseen circumstances,

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:44.870
but I'd like you to endeavor to 
minimize collateral damage.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:50.220
Our relations with the Defense Ministry 
already require a delicate touch.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:51.990
Excuse me.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.360
To hell with the lot of them...

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:01.080
Rin?

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:03.750
Oh, hey!

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.730
Here for the usual ritual?

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:08.560
Yeah, doing the apology circuit.

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:09.560
What about you, Inagi-kun?

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:14.130
Off to the election committee office 
for various application forms.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:16.570
My boss might run for office.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:20.000
Right, it's almost time for gubernatorial 
candidacy announcements.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.000
Hey, do you have some free time?

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:33.210
That's what he said I'd find...

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.530
There are enemies. Enemies trying to kill you.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.030
Get them before they get you!

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:09.380
Thus, just as the redevelopment of 
western Tokyo began to pick up steam,

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.910
a rapid recovery of groundwater 
in the Kanto plains—

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:12.950
Whoa, it's shaking!

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:14.300
Hey, the net!

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.430
Wh-What's going on?

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:28.000
What?

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.060
What's going on?

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:36.280
Why don't you have Hina-chan 
take over the rounds?

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.340
I bet she can get through anything
with that smile of hers.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:41.560
Yeah, I know I lack social skills.

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:44.830
I only told Hinata about 
this side of things, anyway.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:49.750
<b>Second Community Safety Division  
Yamabuki Rin</b>

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.480
Guess you have it rough, too.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.750
So, what I wanted to talk to you about—

00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:51.420
Hang on, sorry.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:52.990
Hello?

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:55.460
We have a sortie request from the Shinagawa PS.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.850
The location is the Kouki Education Academy.

00:10:58.850 --> 00:10:59.630
Huh?

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:03.300
Apparently, a firefighter Willwear 
is destroying the campus.

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:08.580
This way!

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:09.730
This way, everyone!

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.440
I'm going to lower the shutters, okay?

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.590
O-Okay.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:16.630
Everyone to the gym! Hurry!

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:17.760
President?

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.100
I'll make sure there are no 
underclassmen left behind.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:22.410
Yamabuki-kun, stay with the others!

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:26.130
President...

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:36.420
The Willwear is Dainippon Textiles' DSE-4800.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:40.260
It seems to be jury-rigged with 
the Iwasaki ISR-20 module

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.470
that was outlawed two years ago.

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:45.640
The Iwasaki?

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:49.390
Wasn't that developed for personnel 
working to restore quicksand districts?

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:53.590
Yes, it was a refresher option module 
for construction-engineering Willwear.

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:57.010
Those types typically provide 
high-oxygen air or aromatherapy,

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:59.310
but this one utilized gray-zone narcotics

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:02.140
to help users endure harsh working conditions.

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:02.660
I remember now.

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.050
I'll be there ASAP.

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:05.750
I'm close, so it should be soon.

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:09.070
<i>Of all places, why is it at Hinata's school?</i>

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:12.220
Tokyo might soon find 
itself in a difficult position.

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:12.580
Huh?

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:15.440
I am the secretary to a politician, after all.

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:17.620
I hear a lot of things.

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:20.460
Many factions are starting to make their moves...

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.920
Each with their own ideas of justice.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.710
Then, all we have to do is...

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:31.530
President!

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.100
What are you doing here?

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.320
Yamabuki-kun, you followed me?

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:37.810
I thought I might be able to figure 
out the attacker's destination

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:40.110
if I accessed the school's security cameras.

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:48.490
Obtained access to the security cameras.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:50.030
Sending feed to main screen.

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:51.710
I see someone.

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:52.920
A hostage?

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.000
Let's zoom in on a still.

00:12:57.820 --> 00:12:58.810
The boss?!

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:01.050
But she's wearing...

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:05.900
I think she mentioned being proud of having 
a much younger sister at this school.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.730
She must be real smart.

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:09.800
It's a super elite school.

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:11.770
The protective capsule's closing.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.140
The girl's been taken hostage!

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.080
To secure an optimal ejection angle,

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:19.500
the command vehicle will move to Beta 08.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:22.030
Everyone, prepare to sortie.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.260
Roger!

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:37.080
Hinata?

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:38.020
Yes.

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:41.600
She's trapped in the protective capsule 
attached to the attacker's Willwear.

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:43.510
What's the capsule's durability?

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:46.020
IARC rating is level 2.

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:48.590
Is there anyone else we need to rescue? 
Whatever intel you have is fine.

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:52.100
It seems most of the civilians 
have evacuated to the gym,

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:55.100
but they said they lost contact 
with a student named Hachijou.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:13:59.600
Here's our strategy.

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:02.820
After incapacitating the target, 
we gain direct access

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:05.430
to the Willwear and force a system shutdown.

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:07.310
Haruka-chan, Kuroki-kun—

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:08.490
Wait!

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:09.310
What?

00:14:09.310 --> 00:14:14.120
The target's Wear has an MTQ 
1.3 times that of Oscar II's.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.450
There's no guarantee that 
Kuroki-san can incapacitate it.

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:20.360
We'll lure the target to the partially 
collapsed second campus building,

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:22.020
then destroy the building, burying it.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:23.830
Not another reckless plan!

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:25.420
Your methods are too crude!

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:29.030
Besides, if you force a shutdown,

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:33.560
it'll mean cutting off the oxygen 
to the capsule's occupant!

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:36.140
If the rubble isn't cleared 
fast enough, your sister—

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:38.410
We cannot give my sister special treatment.

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:42.110
Minimizing collateral damage is our prio—

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.820
My Fine Familia is capable of 
incapacitating that Wear.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:50.200
With my cutting-edge, advanced Wear unit,

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:54.580
it's possible to minimize collateral damage 
and prioritize civilian safety.

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:58.080
Sure, it's possible.

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:01.710
I am able to maximize that possibility!

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:04.920
Hey, it's not so easy when you're 
out there in the real world.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:06.530
That's no problem!

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:09.690
I've cleared SS-rated simulations!

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:12.690
Fine.

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:16.310
I hereby order you, Kazari Asami, 
to sortie as Oscar VI.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:17.930
Roger!

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:19.680
Hey, boss...

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.640
Vitals, all green.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:28.280
Lock.

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:38.040
Inner unit, begin output.

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:45.000
Oscar VI, set Fine Familia Unit.

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:04.120
<i>I won't do things the way they're used to.</i>

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:07.940
<i>The police are a force of justice!</i>

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:12.500
Oscar VI, data-link to mobile 
assault vehicle confirmed.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:13.860
Request permission to launch.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:14.860
Permission granted.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:15.870
Permission granted.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:16.620
Launching.

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:22.450
Is it Unit 8 that is foolish,

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:25.040
or Japan itself, as a system?

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:31.590
Target confirmed.

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:32.760
Descending.

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:42.720
This is the police!

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.410
Power down the Willwear 
and surrender immediately!

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:47.730
The auto-lock function is off. 
Would you like to enable it?

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:47.730
<b>Combat Help Function  
On       Off  

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:48.850
Huh?

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:50.440
Of course I would.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:52.800
Stabilizer mode is recommended.

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.090
Would you like to enable it?

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:55.060
No!

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:56.600
Is that definitive?

00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:57.700
I said, "No"!

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:02.080
Would you like to record 
footage for use at trial?

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.080
<b>Auto-Memory Function 
On      Off 

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:05.270
Ugh, what's going on?

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:06.330
Kyoukai-san?

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:09.890
Yeah, I thought it would still 
be in initial startup mode.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:12.090
That's what I was trying to fix this morning.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:12.670
Huh?

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:15.360
By default, the Wakaba Group Willwears

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:19.380
come with a helpful assistant function, 
so even normal civilians can use them.

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:21.230
What normal civilian would use this?

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:24.520
It's designed with an eye
toward mass consumption.

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:26.420
I don't care why.

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:27.980
Tell me how to turn it off!

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:27.980
Oscar VI!

